course: dictionary
lesson: 900
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A biter is a person or animal that bites, or tends to bite. The ending -er is a clue: it often means one who does the action, so a runner runs and a biter bites. «Ticks are tiny biters that live in long grass and woods and can spread Lyme disease.» The sentence tells you ticks are small creatures that bite.
explain: Context gives you more clues. The sentence says ticks live in long grass and woods, so biters can be animals, not only people. Lyme disease is a warning that biters can make you ill. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Ticks are tiny creatures that bite" still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. In fishing, a biter is a fish that takes the bait. Read the sentence around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: A biter is a person or animal that bites, or tends to bite.
fact: The ending -er often means one who does the action, so a biter is one that bites.
fact: «Ticks are tiny biters» means ticks are small creatures that bite.
fact: In fishing, a biter is a fish that takes the bait.
fact: «The biter bit» means someone who tried to trick others was tricked themselves.
exercise: «Be careful, he's a biter.» What does biter mean here? | A bright light in the dark | *A person or animal that bites, or tends to bite | A fish that takes the bait | A tool for cutting wood
exercise: In fishing, what is a biter? | A person who fishes at night | A boat with a long net | *A fish that takes the bait | A hook with no bait on it
exercise: When Sam's prank backfired, Mum laughed: «The biter bit!» What does this mean? | A dog bit a postman | *Someone who tried to trick others got tricked themselves | A fish swallowed the hook | Sam ate his lunch too quickly
test: «Ticks are tiny biters that live in long grass and woods.» What are ticks in this sentence? | *Small creatures that bite | Long grass cutters | Tall trees that grow in woods | Gentle pets that sleep all day
test: What clue does the ending -er give in biter? | It means very old | *It means someone or something that does the action | It always means a fish | It means very hungry
exam: Which sentence uses biter in the fishing sense? | «Be careful, the new dog is a biter.» | «Ticks are tiny biters in long grass.» | *«The fish was a sharp-eyed biter that grabbed the worm in one go.» | «The biter bit him after he tried to cheat.»
